    "work": "A Canoa Virou (Brazilian two-stanza traditional form)",
    "historicalRecord": "The traditional song is documented in Pedro Fernandes Tomas, Cancoes Portuguesas, 1934, p. 85; the familiar Brazilian two-stanza form is identified as public domain by Brazilian educational and discographic references.",
    "transcription": "Independent Pianify notation of the public-domain Brazilian form, limited to the two traditional stanzas (A canoa virou / Se eu fosse um peixinho). Pitch order was cross-checked against a reviewed Cifra Club tablature and regional reference scores; third-party files and the later Siri pra ca refrain are not bundled. The left hand is an original Pianify editorial harmonization v1."
